>> title: Congee, Instant Pot
>> category: Soups
>> tags: rice, chicken, chinese, breakfast, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot congee, pressure cooker congee, instant pot jook, instant pot rice porridge, jook, juk, zhou, 粥, rice porridge, plain congee
>> servings: 4
>> dish: congee
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: scallion-pancakes
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — do not open the valve: venting sends a jet of scalding porridge out of the top, and that is a burn
>> step.1: cook the rice in stock — 30 min at high pressure
>> step.2: wait out the natural release 20 min — never the valve, it sprays
>> step.3: stir in the chicken and pepper
>> step.4: season off the heat, and top

Put @jasmine rice{1%cup}(185 g; rinsed until the water runs clear) into the #Instant Pot{} with @chicken stock{8%cups}(1.9 L), @ginger{2%in}(sliced into coins) and @kosher salt{1%tsp}, lock the lid and ~pressure cook{30%min} at high pressure.

Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops on its own. Do not open the valve: venting sends a jet of scalding porridge out of the top.

Stir @&(~1)congee{} with @shredded cooked chicken{1 1/2%cups}(210 g) and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}, on Sauté if it needs loosening or warming through.

Season @&(~1)congee{} off the heat with @soy sauce{1%Tbs} and @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}, and top with @scallions{4}(thinly sliced) and @cilantro{2%Tbs}.
